                                "sense_id": "3e4f78e6-48e4-3b5b-8a1c-fe9ba1bca14c",
                                "text": "In California three rootstock species are in general use. From fairly reliable estimates, about 65 per cent of the cherries grown in the state are grafted on mazzard (Prunus avium); 30 per cent are on mahaleb (P. mahaleb); and 5 per cent on morello (P. cerasus)."
